# Rust-vs-Go perf VERDICT gate — environment-INDEPENDENT competitiveness band.
#
# Each value is a Rust/Go ratio bound, NOT an absolute baseline envelope. A
# ratio is dimensionless, so the same band holds on any host (the old CV-padded
# envelope was baselined on one machine and tripped false FAILs on CI's
# different hardware — a 5× memory WIN read FAIL because its ratio drifted above
# a locally-derived 0.15 cap).
#
# Semantics:
#   *_ratio_min (higher-is-better, throughput): PASS if rust/go >= bound
#       0.85 → Rust within 15% of Go's throughput, or faster, counts as parity.
#   *_ratio_max (lower-is-better, rss/cold/bin): PASS if rust/go <= bound
#       1.15 → Rust within 15% of Go, or leaner/faster/smaller, counts as parity.
# So PASS = "Rust competitive with or better than Go"; FAIL = a genuine
# Rust-slower-than-Go outlier worth a look (informational — the perf job never
# gates the build). REGRESSION detection is the separate same-host run-vs-previous
# diff in examples-perf-sweep.sh, which IS environment-consistent.
#
# `rust-perf.sh --baseline` can still regenerate CV-padded envelopes for LOCAL
# same-host regression gating, but do NOT commit that output here — this file is
# the portable competitiveness gate.

cli.rss_ratio_max = 1.15
cli.coldstart_ratio_max = 1.15
cli.binsize_ratio_max = 1.15
server.rss_ratio_max = 1.15
server.coldstart_ratio_max = 1.15
server.binsize_ratio_max = 1.15
server.throughput_ratio_min = 0.85
live.rss_ratio_max = 1.15
live.coldstart_ratio_max = 1.15
live.binsize_ratio_max = 1.15
live.throughput_ratio_min = 0.85
